<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wamara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wamara is remembered in the traditions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> as the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chwezi">Bachwezi</a>, the semi-legendary dynasty of the kingdom of Kitara. Nkore tradition makes his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhinda">Ruhinda</a> the founder of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinda-dynasty">Hinda dynasty</a>, and Wamara is also venerated as one of the chief spirits of the Chwezi spirit cult. His historicity, like that of the Chwezi kingdom itself, is uncertain.</p></div>
